CM_ "Message names beginning with X_ contain at least one unknown, raw, candidate or otherwise unconfirmed field or interpretation.";
CM_ "DGN-generic RV-C/J1939 database. Broadcast/status BO_ identifiers use source address 0x00. The low source byte must be ignored or replaced by the real node source address. VFrameFormat=J1939PG is included for decoders that support source-address-independent PGN/DGN matching. Priority may also vary between nodes; match on DGN=(CAN_ID>>8)&0x1FFFF rather than the complete 29-bit identifier.";
CM_ BO_ 2482044928 "CONFIRMED battery configuration DGN 0x1F100. BatteryType, ConfiguredCapacity and MaxChargeCurrent are decoded. D6 was consistently 0x0C on this 12 V installation and remains NominalSystemVoltage_Candidate until confirmed on another nominal system voltage.";
CM_ BO_ 2482045952 "CONFIRMED DGN 0x1F104 BatterySOC on D1. D3-D4 are EstimatorRaw_Candidate and remain unconfirmed; 0xFFFF means unavailable in the observed capture.";
CM_ BO_ 2482143232 "CONFIRMED RedVision display mirror: D1-D2 battery current, D3-D4 battery voltage, D5-D6 device current. Display values are rounded relative to native source frames.";
CM_ BO_ 2482143744 "CONFIRMED RedVision input/output-current mirror: D1-D2 AC, D3-D4 vehicle, D5-D6 solar, D7-D8 Manager output. All are LE u16 with A=raw*0.1-1000.";
CM_ BO_ 2482144256 "CONFIRMED RedVision voltage mirror: D1-D2 AC volts at 1 V/count; D3-D4 vehicle, D5-D6 solar, D7-D8 battery/output at 0.1 V/count.";
CM_ BO_ 2549350400 "CONFIRMED firmware-version record. D1-D2 are the little-endian firmware product number, D3 is version major, D4 is version minor, D5-D6 are zero/reserved in observed records, D7 is the firmware record index and D8 is zero/reserved. Display formatting is FW-%04u-%02u-%02u. Confirmed examples include FW-0256-01-14, FW-0256-00-09, FW-0191-03-04 and FW-0323-01-04.";
CM_ BO_ 2549350912 "HIGH CONFIDENCE: D1 day, D2 month, D3-D4 little-endian year. Observed dates were plausible device build/manufacture dates. D5-D8 were 0xFF.";
CM_ BO_ 2549351168 "CONFIRMED segmented ASCII product name. D1 is segment index; D2-D8 are seven ASCII bytes with 0xFF padding. Three observed segments reconstruct 'RedVision Display'.";
CM_ BO_ 2616460544 "HIGH CONFIDENCE structure: D1 record index and D2-D8 stable 56-bit device-unique value, likely serial/UID. Compare against printed serial/About screen to confirm semantics.";
CM_ BO_ 2213808128 "CONFIRMED Manager30 static-configuration DGN 0x1F408. The individual static configuration bytes are unconfirmed. D1-D2 decoding as 30.0 A is retained only as RatedChargeCurrent_Candidate; remaining active bytes stay raw.";
CM_ BO_ 2616332032 "PARTIAL TVMS1280 configuration array. D1 was 0x15 and D2-D7 contained six equal values, matching the six tank inputs. Change one tank sender/type to map each byte and code.";
CM_ BO_ 2617045504 "CONFIRMED DGN 0x1FCF2 is inverter-related data. Its individual fields remain unconfirmed. D1 was observed as item/channel 0x0E, D2-D4 were zero while the inverter was off, and D5-D8 were 0xFF. Do not apply the 0x1FCF0 byte order to this DGN.";
CM_ BO_ 2549942016 "HIGH CONFIDENCE array structure: D1 BaseItem then metadata/status bytes for BaseItem..BaseItem+6. Pages align with 0x1FD02 sensor item IDs. Codes 0xFC, 0xFD and 0xFF remain unresolved.";
CM_ BO_ 2617054208 "HIGH CONFIDENCE array structure, unknown metric: page 0x0C maps Rogue outputs 1-7 and page 0x13 maps outputs 8-10. Values were zero in the capture. Test with a loaded/dimmed output.";
CM_ BO_ 2617049088 "CONFIRMED DGN 0x1FD00 carries TVMS states. The numeric state-code meanings are not yet confirmed. All value-table labels remain candidates, including observed code 0x24 on configured inactive output/inverter channels.";
CM_ BO_ 2617053696 "CONFIRMED DGN 0x1FD12 carries output and input state data. D1 is the page/base selector. Pages 0x0C and 0x13 map Rogue outputs; pages 0x1A and 0x21 contain additional input/state data and remain exposed as raw values.";




CM_ "RedVision / TVMS CAN bridge - signals reflect ONLY what the ESPHome components decode and transmit.";
CM_ BU_ Bridge "This ESP32 / ESPHome CAN bridge. Source address is configurable (host_address, default 0x22).";
CM_ BO_ 2482045440 "29-bit extended IDs. Receivers key on DGN=(ID>>8)&0x1FFFF and source address=ID&0xFF. Message IDs here have the source-address byte (low 8 bits) set to 0x00 so one definition matches a DGN from ANY source address; OR the real source byte in when transmitting/filtering. Observed source addresses: Manager30 0x01, BatterySensor 0x08, RedVision displays 0x20/0x21, TVMS1280 0x24, TVMSRogue 0x30, Bridge 0x22.";
CM_ BO_ 2482819072 "Paginated history array. PageIndex (D1) selects the block; absolute hour index = PageIndex*7 + SlotN. Value 255 (0xFF) means no data.";
CM_ BO_ 2482819584 "Paginated history array. Absolute day index = PageIndex*7 + SlotN. 255 = no data. Combined with the daily-high page into the SOC Daily Range entity.";
CM_ BO_ 2482820096 "Paginated history array. Absolute day index = PageIndex*7 + SlotN. 255 = no data.";
CM_ BO_ 2213741568 "Manager30 clock/status response. D1 bits 7-3 encode day-1; D1 bits 2-0 encode weekday (1=Monday through 7=Sunday). D2=month, D3-D4=year little-endian, D5=hour, D6=minute, D7=second, D8 is normally 0xFF. Observed from source address 0x01.";
CM_ BO_ 2214385152 "Solar generation history, 4 pages x 3 days = 12 days. Day 0 = today, Day 1..11 = previous days, in Wh. Requested via REQ_0FFCD6 (RTR).";
CM_ BO_ 2617049088 "DGN 0x1FD00 is shared by TVMS1280 (SA 0x24) and TVMSRogue (SA 0x30). Confirmed array layout: BaseItem in D1 followed by State_Plus0..6 for channels BaseItem..BaseItem+6. TVMS1280 channel map: 0x01-0x03 Digital Inputs 1-3, 0x04-0x0D Outputs 1-10, 0x0E Inverter, 0x0F Master. TVMSRogue channel map: 0x01-0x08 Input Buttons 1-8, 0x0B Master, 0x0C-0x15 Outputs 1-10. State-code interpretations remain unconfirmed.";
CM_ BO_ 2617049600 "DGN 0x1FD02 shared by TVMS1280 (SA 0x24) and TVMSRogue (SA 0x30), multiplexed by ItemId (D1). Item codes do not collide between the two devices, so one definition serves both.";
CM_ BO_ 2617053696 "DGN 0x1FD12 output/input state data is multiplexed by LevelPageId (D1). Existing output-page signals are retained for pages 0x0C and 0x13; input/state pages 0x1A and 0x21 remain raw pending exact channel mapping.";
CM_ BO_ 2617044992 "TVMS1280 inverter status. InverterState (D1) is on/off when InverterItemId (D2) == 0x0E.";
CM_ BO_ 2415710208 "RTR remote-request frame (no payload, DLC 8). Polls the battery for SOC hourly history; reply is BATT_1FCD0.";
CM_ BO_ 2415710720 "RTR remote-request frame (no payload). Polls SOC daily-low history; reply is BATT_1FCD2.";
CM_ BO_ 2415711232 "RTR remote-request frame (no payload). Polls SOC daily-high history; reply is BATT_1FCD4.";
CM_ BO_ 2415711744 "RTR remote-request frame (no payload). Polls the manager for solar history; reply is MGR_1FCD6.";
CM_ BO_ 2415068160 "CONFIRMED Manager30 set-clock command. Actual CAN ID is 0x0FF304<source_address>; this DBC leaves the source byte at 0x00, so OR in the transmitting host address. D1=((day-1)<<3)|weekday, where weekday 1=Monday through 7=Sunday. D2=month, D3-D4=year little-endian, D5=hour, D6=minute, D7=second, D8=0x00. Confirmed example: ID 0x0FF304FA, B2 06 EA 07 10 23 29 00 set 23 June 2026 16:35:41 Tuesday. Manager30 confirmed approximately 230 ms later on 0x03F30401.";
CM_ BO_ 2617036288 "CONFIRMED history-clear command. Actual CAN ID is 0x1BFCCE<source_address>; this compact DBC leaves the source byte at 0x00. D1 selects the history dataset, D2 must be 0xFC, and D3-D8 must be 0xFF. Confirmed selectors: 0xD0=Hourly SOC history (reply DGN 0x1FCD0), 0xD2=Daily Low SOC history (reply 0x1FCD2), 0xD4=Daily High SOC history (reply 0x1FCD4), and 0xD6=Solar Energy history (reply 0x1FCD6). Observed from RedVision source 0x20 as CAN ID 0x1BFCCE20. No separate acknowledgement was identified; deletion was confirmed by reading back zeroed history pages.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryDataset "History dataset selector: D0=Hourly SOC, D2=Daily Low SOC, D4=Daily High SOC, D6=Solar Energy.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryClearCommand "Clear/delete command marker. Confirmed value is 0xFC.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryReservedD3 "Required constant 0xFF in confirmed clear-history commands.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryReservedD4 "Required constant 0xFF in confirmed clear-history commands.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryReservedD5 "Required constant 0xFF in confirmed clear-history commands.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryReservedD6 "Required constant 0xFF in confirmed clear-history commands.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryReservedD7 "Required constant 0xFF in confirmed clear-history commands.";
CM_ SG_ 2617036288 HistoryReservedD8 "Required constant 0xFF in confirmed clear-history commands.";
CM_ SG_ 2482045440 BatteryCurrent "Signed via offset: A = raw/1000 - 1000. Positive = charging, negative = discharging.";
CM_ SG_ 2213677568 OutputCurrent "A = raw/1000 - 1000.";
CM_ SG_ 2482143232 BatteryCurrentDisplay "Display rebroadcast value: A = raw/10 - 1000.";
CM_ BO_ 2213676032 "Native Manager30 AC input. ACInputCurrent D1-D4 (raw/1000 - 1000 A, 0.001 A resolution), ACInputVoltage D5-D6 (1 V/count). Example 0x03F20401 E8 42 0F 00 EF 00 FD FF -> 0.168 A, 239 V. Preferred over the display rebroadcast 0x1F282 which is rounded to 0.1 A.";
CM_ SG_ 2213676032 ACInputCurrent "A = raw/1000 - 1000.";
CM_ BO_ 2213676544 "Native Manager30 vehicle input, ~10 Hz. Confirmed from capture (224 frames): current D1-D4, voltage D5-D6, mode trigger D8. Example 0x03F20601 40 42 0F 00 31 31 FC 01 -> 0.000 A, 12.593 V, trigger 0x01.";
CM_ SG_ 2213676544 VehicleInputCurrent "Confirmed: A = raw/1000 - 1000. Constant 0 A across the capture.";
CM_ SG_ 2213676544 VehicleInputVoltage "Confirmed: V = raw/1000. Ranged 12.552-12.629 V across the capture.";
CM_ BO_ 2482143744 "RedVision display mirror, ~1 Hz. DisplayVehicleCurrent (D3-D4) and ManagerOutputCurrentDisplay (D7-D8) both scale 0.1, offset -1000.";
CM_ BO_ 2482144256 "RedVision display mirror of the Manager30 vehicle input voltage, ~1 Hz. D3-D4, scale 0.1 V. Example 0x13F28420 F1 00 7D 00 ... -> 12.5 V.";
CM_ SG_ 2617049600 RogueInputCurrent "CONFIRMED: DGN 0x1FD02, page 0x16, D4-D5 little-endian. Rogue input current in amperes = raw * 0.001. Controlled capture rose from approximately 0.05 A to 8.781 A and returned to approximately 0.05 A.";


CM_ BO_ 2616460288 "CONFIRMED DGN 0x1F404 periodic device identity record. D1-D4 are the unsigned little-endian decimal serial-number prefix YYMMDDNNNN. D5-D6 are the unsigned little-endian decimal factory serial suffix SSSS. The complete serial printed on the device is formatted as prefix zero-padded to 10 decimal digits, a hyphen, then suffix zero-padded to 4 decimal digits: %010u-%04u. D7 is the confirmed device type. D8 remains an unresolved subtype/family byte.";
CM_ SG_ 2616460288 SerialNumberPrefix "CONFIRMED first component of the factory serial number. Unsigned little-endian uint32, displayed as exactly 10 decimal digits in the form YYMMDDNNNN.";
CM_ SG_ 2616460288 SerialNumberSuffix "CONFIRMED second component of the factory serial number. Unsigned little-endian uint16, displayed as exactly 4 decimal digits SSSS. It is part of the printed production serial number, not an installation sequence.";
CM_ SG_ 2616460288 DeviceSubtypeRaw "Unresolved raw subtype/family byte. Observed values: 0xFF Manager30 and BMS Battery Sensor, 0x02 RedVision Display, 0x00 TVMS1280 and TVMS Rogue.";


VAL_ 2616460288 DeviceType 1 "Manager30" 3 "BMSBatterySensor" 12 "RedVisionDisplay" 14 "TVMS1280" 22 "TVMSRogue" ;

CM_ SG_ 2482044928 NominalSystemVoltage_Candidate "Observed literal 12 V. Candidate until tested on another nominal system voltage.";
CM_ SG_ 2482045952 EstimatorRaw_Candidate "Dynamic raw estimator. 0xFFFF was the unavailable value; meaning unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 2549351168 ProductNameChar1 "ASCII byte; concatenate Char1..Char7 in segment-index order and ignore 0xFF padding.";
CM_ SG_ 2616460288 DeviceType "CONFIRMED device-type code: 1 Manager30, 3 BMS Battery Sensor, 12 RedVision Display, 14 TVMS1280, 22 TVMS Rogue.";

