CM_ "READ-WRITE UPDATE: configuration object transport, CRC-32C, direct setting commands, DGN 0x1F108 readback and confirmed serialized-object enums were added from readwrite.csv and controlled changed-setting captures 1 through 5.";
CM_ "SERIALIZED CONFIG OBJECTS: object 2 is the main device/system configuration; object 3 is RedVision display/UI configuration. Header +0x04 is uint32 object length and +0x08 is whole-object CRC-32C. Calculate the object CRC across ObjectLength bytes after replacing bytes +0x08..+0x0B with zero.";
CM_ "SERIALIZED CONFIG INTEGER TAGGING: immediate integer stored = actual value*4+1; decode actual=(stored-1)/4. Pointers are 4-byte aligned. String-alignment bytes can change without representing settings.";
CM_ "The variable-length object contents cannot be represented as fixed DBC signals. Named VAL_TABLE_ entries and this database comments preserve the confirmed object enum mappings; the companion read-write report contains record-level details.";

CM_ BO_ 2482046976 "CONFIRMED TVMS1280 and TVMS Rogue DGN 0x1F108 priority-4 form. D1 bits2-4 are the load-disconnect trigger, D2-D3 disconnect voltage in millivolts, D4-D5 reconnect voltage in millivolts, D6 disconnect SOC percent and D7 reconnect SOC percent. D1 low/high flag bits remain unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 2482046976 LoadDisconnectTrigger "Confirmed enum: 0 Always, 1 BMS Voltage, 2 BMS SOC, 3 Never, 4 Voltage.";
CM_ SG_ 2482046976 ConfigFlagsLowRaw "Unresolved D1 bits0-1.";
CM_ SG_ 2482046976 ConfigHighFlagsRaw "Unresolved D1 bits5-7; observed high bits are normally set.";

CM_ BO_ 2399338496 "DGN request. Actual CAN ID is 0x0F03<destination><requester>. D1-D2 contain the requested 17-bit DGN little-endian. Example 04 F4 requests DGN 0x1F404.";
CM_ BO_ 2390818816 "Configuration-object write data. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E81<device><tool>. Each frame contributes eight sequential bytes to the block committed by the following 0x0E88 service.";
CM_ BO_ 2390949888 "Pre-write query observed before object writes. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E83<device><tool>. Both arguments were zero in captures. Exact purpose remains unconfirmed.";
CM_ BO_ 2391080960 "Object select. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E85<device><tool>. D1 selects the object. Confirmed configurator objects: 2 main device/system configuration, 3 RedVision display/UI configuration.";
CM_ BO_ 2391146496 "Block read request. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E86<device><tool>. D1-D4 offset and D5-D8 requested length are uint32 little-endian.";
CM_ BO_ 2391212032 "Prepare/open object for writing. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E87<device><tool>. Captures used offset 0 and second argument 0x7FFFFFFF. Exact argument semantics remain candidates.";
CM_ BO_ 2391277568 "Commit the preceding 0x0E81 data block. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E88<device><tool>. D1-D4 destination offset; D5-D8 CRC-32C/Castagnoli of exactly the preceding block bytes.";
CM_ BO_ 2391343104 "Close the selected configuration object. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E89<device><tool>.";
CM_ BO_ 2391408640 "Apply/activate the written configuration. Actual CAN ID is 0x0E8A<device><tool>. Apply semantics are strongly supported by sequence position but not independently confirmed.";
CM_ BO_ 2189426688 "Directed object-service acknowledgement. Actual CAN ID is 0x0280<requester><device>. D1=1 was busy/in progress and D1=0 complete/ready; D3 echoes the service opcode.";
CM_ BO_ 2189492224 "Configuration-object read data. Actual CAN ID is 0x0281<requester><device>. Concatenate payloads in frame order and truncate to the byte count from 0x0284.";
CM_ BO_ 2189688832 "Read block trailer. Actual CAN ID is 0x0284<requester><device>. D1-D4 returned byte count; D5-D8 CRC-32C/Castagnoli of exactly that many returned bytes. The same frame type is also seen after the unconfirmed 0x0E83 query.";
CM_ SG_ 2391277568 BlockWriteCRC32C "CRC-32C/Castagnoli, reflected polynomial 0x82F63B78, init 0xFFFFFFFF, xorout 0xFFFFFFFF.";
CM_ SG_ 2189688832 BlockTrailerCRC32C "CRC-32C/Castagnoli, reflected polynomial 0x82F63B78, init 0xFFFFFFFF, xorout 0xFFFFFFFF.";

CM_ BO_ 2399142144 "Manager30 addressed configuration command. Actual ID is 0x0F0001<tool>. Configurator format is D2=0, D3=3, D4=0 and D5-D8 uint32 little-endian value.";
CM_ BO_ 2399143936 "Battery Sensor addressed configuration command. Actual ID is 0x0F0008<tool>. Configurator format is D2=0, D3=3, D4=0 and D5-D8 uint32 little-endian value.";
CM_ BO_ 2399151104 "TVMS1280 command. Actual ID is 0x0F0024<tool>. Commands 0x3A-0x3E set load-disconnect fields. Command 0xCB controls channel state using D4 channel and D5 state.";
CM_ BO_ 2399154176 "TVMS Rogue command. Actual ID is 0x0F0030<tool>. Commands 0x3A-0x3E set load-disconnect fields. Command 0xCB sets on/off and 0x5A sets absolute output level using D4 channel and D5 value.";
CM_ BO_ 2399468032 "Direct-setting acknowledgement from a configured device to tool address 0xFA. Actual ID is 0x0F04FA<device>. D1=1 was observed for accepted writes and D2 echoes the command ID.";
CM_ SG_ 2399142144 VehicleInputTrigger "Confirmed values: 1=12 V, 3=Ignition, 5=On. Auto and 24 V remain menu-order candidates 0 and 2.";
CM_ SG_ 2399143936 SetBatteryType "Lithium value 4 is directly observed. Values 0-3 follow the configurator menu order and remain less strongly confirmed.";
CM_ SG_ 2399151104 Channel "TVMS1280 channel IDs: 0x04-0x0D outputs 1-10, 0x0E inverter, 0x0F master.";
CM_ SG_ 2399154176 ChannelOnOff "TVMS Rogue channel IDs: 0x0B master, 0x0C-0x15 outputs 1-10.";
CM_ SG_ 2399154176 ChannelLevel "TVMS Rogue channel IDs: 0x0B master, 0x0C-0x15 outputs 1-10.";

